      "hints": [
        "Express the volume as $V = 40000h$ and state $\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}V}{\\mathrm{d}h} = 40000$.",
        "Write the net rate $\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}V}{\\mathrm{d}t} = 50000 - 600h$ and use the chain rule to show $200\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}h}{\\mathrm{d}t} = 250 - 3h$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Express the volume of water in the tank with base area $40000\\text{ cm}^2$ and depth $h$ cm:\n$$V = 40000h \\implies \\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}V}{\\mathrm{d}h} = 40000$$",
        "Write the net rate of change of volume:\n$$\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}V}{\\mathrm{d}t} = \\text{Inflow} - \\text{Outflow} = 50000 - 600h$$",
        "Apply the chain rule connecting $\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}h}{\\mathrm{d}t}$ and $\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}V}{\\mathrm{d}t}$:\n$$\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}V}{\\mathrm{d}t} = \\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}V}{\\mathrm{d}h} \\cdot \\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}h}{\\mathrm{d}t} \\implies 40000\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}h}{\\mathrm{d}t} = 50000 - 600h$$",
        "Divide both sides by $200$:\n$$\\dfrac{40000}{200}\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}h}{\\mathrm{d}t} = \\dfrac{50000}{200} - \\dfrac{600}{200}h$$\n$$200\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}h}{\\mathrm{d}t} = 250 - 3h$$"
      ],
