      "hints": [
        "Separate variables: $\\int \\dfrac{1}{250 - 3h}\\,\\mathrm{d}h = \\int \\dfrac{1}{200}\\,\\mathrm{d}t$.",
        "Integrate to $-\\dfrac{1}{3}\\ln|250 - 3h| = \\dfrac{t}{200} + C$, find $C$ using $t = 0, h = 50$, and find $t$ when $h = 80$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Separate variables in $200\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}h}{\\mathrm{d}t} = 250 - 3h$:\n$$\\dfrac{1}{250 - 3h}\\,\\mathrm{d}h = \\dfrac{1}{200}\\,\\mathrm{d}t$$",
        "Integrate both sides:\n$$\\int \\dfrac{1}{250 - 3h}\\,\\mathrm{d}h = \\int \\dfrac{1}{200}\\,\\mathrm{d}t$$\n$$-\\dfrac{1}{3}\\ln|250 - 3h| = \\dfrac{t}{200} + C$$",
        "Apply the initial condition $h = 50$ when $t = 0$:\n$$-\\dfrac{1}{3}\\ln|250 - 3(50)| = 0 + C$$\n$$-\\dfrac{1}{3}\\ln(100) = C \\implies C = -\\dfrac{1}{3}\\ln 100$$",
        "Substitute $C$ back into the solution:\n$$-\\dfrac{1}{3}\\ln(250 - 3h) = \\dfrac{t}{200} - \\dfrac{1}{3}\\ln 100$$\n$$\\dfrac{t}{200} = \\dfrac{1}{3}\\ln 100 - \\dfrac{1}{3}\\ln(250 - 3h) = \\dfrac{1}{3}\\ln\\left(\\dfrac{100}{250 - 3h}\\right)$$\n$$t = \\dfrac{200}{3}\\ln\\left(\\dfrac{100}{250 - 3h}\\right)$$",
        "Substitute $h = 80$ to find the time:\n$$250 - 3(80) = 250 - 240 = 10$$\n$$\\dfrac{100}{250 - 3(80)} = \\dfrac{100}{10} = 10$$\n$$t = \\dfrac{200}{3}\\ln(10)$$",
        "Evaluate numerically:\n$$\\ln 10 \\approx 2.302585$$\n$$t = \\dfrac{200}{3}(2.302585) \\approx 153.5057 \\dots$$",
        "Round correct to 2 significant figures:\n$$t = 150 \\text{ minutes}$$"
